**2.F.6<sup>A</sup>** Suppose that  $x(p, w)$  is homogeneous of degree zero. Show that the weak axiom holds if and only if for some  $w > 0$  and all  $p, p'$  we have  $p' \cdot x(p, w) > w$  whenever  $p \cdot x(p', w) \leq w$  and  $x(p', w) \neq x(p, w)$ .

**2.F.7<sup>B</sup>** In text.

**2.F.8<sup>A</sup>** Let  $\hat{s}_{/k}(p, w) = [p_k/x_{/k}(p, w)]s_{/k}(p, w)$  be the substitution terms in elasticity form. Express  $\hat{s}_{/k}(p, w)$  in terms of  $e_{/k}(p, w)$ ,  $e_{/w}(p, w)$ , and  $b_k(p, w)$ .

