$$x(p) = \frac{1}{p \cdot \nabla v(p)} \nabla v(p).$$

Note that this is a completely symmetric expression. Thus, direct (Walrasian) demand is the normalized derivative of indirect utility, and indirect demand is the normalized derivative of direct utility.

