(a) Argue that when  $E[\theta] \geq r > \theta$ , there are now two competitive equilibria: one with  $w^* = E[\theta]$  and  $\Theta^* = [\theta, \bar{\theta}]$  and one with  $w^* = \theta$  and  $\Theta^* = \emptyset$ . Also show that when  $\theta \geq r$  the unique competitive equilibrium is  $w^* = E[\theta]$  and  $\Theta^* = [\theta, \bar{\theta}]$ , and when  $r > E[\theta]$  the unique competitive equilibrium is  $w^* = \theta$  and  $\Theta^* = \emptyset$ .

