2. Note, in particular, that the budget sets of the consumers may well extend outside the box.

3. There are other feasible allocations that are simultaneously affordable; but in these allocations some resources are not consumed by either consumer, and thus they cannot be depicted in an Edgeworth box. Because of the nonsatiation assumption to be made on preferences, we will not have to worry about such allocations.

